# Implementation Plan - Dashboard Advancements (YoY, Trajectory, Comparison, Intensity)

This plan outlines the steps to add advanced analytical features and fix critical logic bugs in the Carbon Intensity module.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. YoY Variance Indicators (Hero Card)
- **Calculation**: In [loadDashboardData](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/dashboard.js#240-306), if a specific year is selected, identify the previous year's total emissions from `summaryData`.
- **UI**: Add a `VarianceBadge` component next to Gross Emissions and Intensity values.
- **Visuals**: Green for decrease, Red for increase, Grey for no change/no data.

### 2. Target Trajectory (Trend Chart)
- **Logic**: Use the `baseYear` (start point) and [goal](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/server/routes/dashboard.py#241-257) (end point) states.
- **Interpolation**: Create a "Trajectory" data series by calculating a linear path from the Base Year emissions value to the Target Goal value in 2030.
- **UI**: Add a dashed line named "Net Zero Path" to the Line Chart.

### 3. Comparison View
- **Mechanism**: Introduce a "Compare" mode toggle.
- **Logic**: 
    - When "Compare Mode" is active, fetch data for all facilities within the selected Activity/Division.
    - Transform `trendData` to have many series (one per facility) instead of a single Scope 1+2 sum.
- **UI**: Add a toggle button in the header. Update `LineChartWrapper` to handle dynamic numbers of lines.

### 4. Carbon Intensity Logic & Bug Fixes
- **Backend ([dashboard.py](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/server/routes/dashboard.py))**:
    - Update `/intensity-stats` to join with the [Facility](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/server/models.py#32-48) table.
    - Implement `activity` and `division` filtering for production and emissions queries.
- **Frontend ([CarbonIntensity.jsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx))**:
    - Correct Hero Card labels:
        - Carbon Intensity: `tCO₂e / bbl` → `kg CO₂e / BOE`
        - Methane Intensity: `tCH₄ / BOE` → `kg CH₄ / BOE`
    - Standardize units across all charts (using kg/BOE as the primary metric).
    - Ensure [formatNumber](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/utils/formatters.js#20-35) precision is appropriate for kg/BOE (e.g., 2 decimals for CO2, 4 for CH4).

---

## Technical Details

### Dashboard Enhanced
- Add `isCompareMode` state.
- Update [loadDashboardData](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/dashboard.js#240-306) to handle multi-series fetching for comparison.
- Calculate `prevYearStats` for YoY logic.
- Generate `trajectoryPoints` for the goal line.

### Backend Routing
- Update `/summary` to support `groupBy=facility`.
- Update `/intensity-stats` to joined queries with organizational filters.

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Select 2024 and verify the YoY badge correctly compares with 2023.
- Set a Goal for 2030 and verify the dashed line appears on the trend chart.
- Toggle "Compare Mode" and check if multiple lines appear (one for each region).
- Filter Carbon Intensity by "EP" and verify numbers change (Fixing the filter bug).
- Verify Carbon Intensity units match "kg/BOE" in the UI.

### 5. Styling Region-Field in Dropdowns
- **[CustomDropdown.jsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/components/CustomDropdown.jsx)**:
    - Modify to support a [renderOption](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/dashboard.js#130-140) logic for the selected display.
    - Add logic to automatically handle `subLabel` if provided in the option object.
- **Dropdown Options**:
    - Update region options in [DashboardEnhanced.jsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/pages/DashboardEnhanced.jsx), [CarbonIntensity.jsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx), and Scope Forms to use: `{ value, label, subLabel }`.
    - > [!IMPORTANT]
    - > Do NOT change the region management dropdowns in [ManageData.jsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx).
- **Styling**:
    - Update [CustomDropdown.css](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/components/CustomDropdown.css) to style `.sub-label` with a smaller font and grey color.

---

## Technical Details (Dropdown Styling)
- **Component Change**: 
    ```javascript
    const display = renderOption ? renderOption(selectedOption) : (
        selectedOption?.subLabel ? (
            <>{selectedOption.label} <span className="sub-label">-{selectedOption.subLabel}</span></>
        ) : selectedOption?.label || placeholder
    );
    ```
- **Option Change**:
    ```javascript
    { value: f.id, label: f.name, subLabel: f.field }
    ```
